\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Who puts his trust
\par In God most just
\par Hath built his house securely;
\par He who relies
\par On Jesus Christ,
\par Heaven shall be his most surely:
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Then fixed on Thee
\par My trust shall be,
\par For Thy truth cannot alter;
\par While mine Thou art,
\par Not death's worst smart
\par Shall make my courage falter.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Though fiercest foes
\par My course oppose,
\par A dauntless front I'll show them;
\par My champion Thou,
\par Lord Christ, art now,
\par Who soon shalt overthrow them!
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And if but Thee
\par I have in me,
\par With Thy good gifts and Spirit,
\par Nor death nor hell,
\par I know full well,
\par Shall hurt me, through Thy merit.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I rest me here
\par Without a fear-
\par By Thee shall aall be given
\par That I can need,
\par O Friend indeed,
\par For this life or for heaven.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par O make me true,
\par My heart renew,
\par My soul and flesh deliver!
\par Lord, hear my prayer,
\par And in Thy care
\par Keep me in peace for ever.
\par                  Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
